\f0\fs24 Low-Level Design (LLD) \'97 Mid Office Axiom\par
\par
Overview\par
- Project: Mid-office-axiom (React + TypeScript + Vite)\par
- Purpose: Underwriting / claims / mid-office workflow UI\par
- Key tech: React, TypeScript, Vite, MUI, React Router, React Hook Form, Redux-style store with thunks, Jest\par
\par
High-level Architecture\par
- SPA built with React + Vite.\par
- Router: React Router; protected routes via ProtectedRoute.\par
- UI: MUI components, custom UI primitives in src/components/ui.\par
- State: Centralized store under src/store with thunks in src/store/thunks.\par
- Network: src/services contains api.ts, apiConfig.ts, and endpoints.ts.\par
- Modules: feature folders under src/modules (Login, DRS, Grievance, Group, Landing, Retail, QuickLinks, etc.).\par
\par
Important Files and Paths\par
- Entry: src/main.tsx \'97 app bootstrap\par
- Root layout & routes: src/routes/RootLayout.tsx, src/routes/AppRoutes.tsx, src/routes/routes.ts\par
- App container: src/App.tsx\par
- Modules: src/modules/* (per-folder feature components)\par
- UI primitives: src/components/ui/* (Button, TextField, Checkbox, etc.)\par
- Services: src/services/api.ts, src/services/apiConfig.ts, src/services/endpoints.ts\par
- Store: src/store/*, src/store/thunks/*, and src/store/hooks.ts\par
- Hooks: src/hooks/* (e.g., useAppContext.ts, useColumnConfig.ts)\par
- Validations & messages: src/validations, src/config/errorMessages.ts\par
- Assets: src/assets/ (logos, illustrations)\par
- Tests: src/setupTests.ts, jest.config.cjs and tsconfig.jest.json\par
\par
Module: Login\par
- Key files:\par
  - src/modules/Login/Login.tsx\par
- Responsibilities:\par
  - Render login form (React Hook Form + MUI custom fields)\par
  - Validate credentials, dispatch loginThunk from src/store/thunks/authThunk\par
  - Persist token, username, password, businessType to localStorage\par
  - Optionally dispatch fetchMastersForSession (master-data thunk)\par
  - Navigate to inbox using getInboxPath\par
- Sequence:\par
  1. User submits form\par
  2. loginThunk dispatched -> API call\par
  3. On success: store token; dispatch fetchMastersForSession (if required)\par
  4. Navigate to inbox route\par
\par
Authentication & Session\par
- Thunks: authThunk (login), sessionMastersThunk (fetchMastersForSession)\par
- Token storage: localStorage keys: token, username, password, businessType\par
- Protected routes: ProtectedRoute.tsx checks auth token and/or store state\par
- API client: api.ts uses apiConfig.ts for base URL and interceptors (attach token header)\par
\par
State Management (Store)\par
- Structure:\par
  - store/slices or similar for feature slices\par
  - store/thunks/* for async operations\par
  - store/hooks.ts for useAppDispatch and typed useSelector\par
- Common slices:\par
  - auth \'97 login status, user info, token\par
  - sessionMasters \'97 master data required across app\par
  - inbox \'97 list of tasks, filters, pagination\par
  - ui \'97 global UI states (loading overlays, toasts)\par
\par
API Design & Endpoints\par
- Single API layer at src/services/api.ts with helper endpoints.ts.\par
- Responsibilities: one place for HTTP client, request/response normalization, retry/backoff and error handling\par
- Example endpoints: POST /auth/login, GET /masters/session, GET /inbox/tasks\par
\par
Routing\par
- AppRoutes.tsx composes application routes.\par
- ProtectedRoute.tsx enforces authentication and role/business-type routing.\par
- getInboxPath(businessType) returns route to the business-specific inbox (e.g., retail)\par
\par
Components & UI\par
- Atomic primitives in src/components/ui (TextField, Checkbox, Button).\par
- Page-level components in src/modules/* act as containers and orchestrate data fetching.\par
- Shared layout components in src/layout (headers, footers, sidebars)\par
\par
Hooks\par
- useAppContext.ts \'97 application-level context and helpers\par
- useColumnConfig.ts \'97 column configuration logic and persistence\par
\par
Utilities\par
- src/utils contains style helpers, constants, and small helpers (e.g., centerFlex, columnFlex)\par
- src/validations centralizes React Hook Form validation schemas\par
- src/config/errorMessages.json and src/config/errorMessages.ts centralize textual errors\par
\par
Data Models (TypeScript types)\par
- Types stored under src/store/types or src/types: User/Auth response, Master data, Task/Inbox item\par
\par
Error Handling\par
- Thunks should try/catch and return standardized error objects to UI\par
- Global API error interceptor to handle 401 (session expiry) and refresh/redirect to login\par
- UI: snackbar/toast for transient messages; inline helper text for form errors\par
\par
Testing\par
- Unit tests: Jest + React Testing Library\par
- src/setupTests.ts contains test setup\par
\par
Build & Run\par
- Dev: npm run dev (Vite)\par
- Build: npm run build\par
- Test: npm run test\par
\par
Deployment\par
- Vite build output -> static hosting (Netlify, S3 + CloudFront, or similar)\par
- Environment-specific apiConfig base URLs\par
\par
Non-Functional Considerations\par
- Performance: lazy-load route-level modules, memoize heavy lists\par
- Security: never persist plaintext passwords in production, use secure HTTP-only cookies or secure storage\par
- Accessibility: follow MUI accessibility defaults, add aria-* where needed\par
\par
Open Implementation Notes (repo-specific)\par
- src/modules/Login/Login.tsx currently uses a USE_MOCK_LOGIN flag; adjust based on environment\par
- fetchMastersForSession is used post-login \'97 ensure its data shape and storage in sessionMasters slice\par
- Confirm the exact slice/file names under src/store and update this doc if they differ\par
